text:
nora-docs: opened PR for onprem installer docs: small add about KMS/HSM proxying when customers run an SNI proxy in front of HSM/KMS appliances. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4891

raj-eng: summary: sealed installs sometimes need a transparent proxy that rewrites SNI or routes by port. we should include a minimal nginx stream example and a note about TLS validation.

nora-docs: added tiny nginx stream snippet in the PR and a short docs blurb:```nginx
stream {
  server {
    listen 443;
    proxy_pass internal-kms:443;
    proxy_ssl_server_name on;
    proxy_ssl_name kms.redwood.ai;
  }
}
```

olivia-sre: add a security callout: if you use proxy_ssl_name to present the public name, ensure the proxy has a valid cert for kms.redwood.ai signed by the customer's trust root. otherwise the installer will fail TLS checks. also mention testing with `openssl s_client -connect proxy:443 -servername kms.redwood.ai`.

mike-cs: customer case: their HSM vendor required a vendor PKCS#11 module loaded early in boot. can we document adding vendor libs into the offline bundle and a systemd unit to load them before the installer chroot? small unit example would help.

raj-eng: added short systemd unit in PR:```ini
[Unit]
Description=Load vendor pkcs11
Before=containerd.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/sbin/modprobe vendor_pkcs11
RemainAfterExit=yes
```

nora-docs: thanks. i've included a short troubleshooting line: "if installer chroot fails with PKCS#11 open errors, ensure vendor module present in offline bundle and visible under /lib or /usr/lib in chroot." deploy-bot: docs-lint passed, linkcheck queued.

olivia-sre: lgtm, small wording tweak around where to place libs for alpine vs deb/rpm.

nora-docs: will squash and merge after linkcheck. tagging @mike-cs for customer follow-up.
